-- #1956 / #1937's remainder, THE ACCEPT DIRECTION: a MULTI-ARGUMENT structured
-- declared context selects PER CALL SITE, from the dict the caller built, and
-- the answer does not depend on `impl` declaration order.
--
-- Hand-derived from DICT-SEMANTICS §3 BEFORE running anything.  `f`'s context is
-- the 2-ary predicate `Conv (Wrap a) b`, and the body goal IS that predicate, so
-- `(d_pi : pi) in P` holds and (assum) applies -- and §3's precedence clause
-- ("assum/super takes precedence; inst fires only when no assumption matches")
-- forbids the body from committing to an impl of its own.  Each call site
-- discharges its own instantiated goal by (inst): `f (Wrap 5) True` grounds to
-- `Conv (Wrap Int) Bool` and `f (Wrap 'c') 7` to `Conv (Wrap Char) Int`, two
-- singleton matching sets, two different impls.  So the two calls must print
-- `wrap-int-bool` and `wrap-char-int` respectively, i.e. `wrap-int-bool/wrap-char-int`.
-- (The two calls are joined with `/` rather than `|` only because `|` is
-- diff_compiler_dict_semantics.sh's own TABLE field separator.)
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS PINS, AND WHY IT IS NOT ITS SIBLINGS' DUPLICATE.  The two
-- `s-multiparam-structured-*` rows both fix the predicate's SECOND argument to
-- `Int`, so lead-argument-only keying and whole-vector keying are
-- indistinguishable on them.  Here the two call sites differ at BOTH positions,
-- which is what makes the vector -- not the lead -- the thing that has to select.
--
-- MEASURED at the sprint base `e4587a04` on this tree, cold built:
-- `run` printed `wrap-int-bool/wrap-int-bool` at exit 0 -- the FIRST impl's body
-- for both calls, because `registerPredGiven` matched a single-subject
-- `[subject]` vector and returned `()` for anything longer, so `entailAssum`
-- could never see this predicate, `entail` fell to `entailInst`, and the body was
-- statically committed to the ABSTRACTION-time pick while both callers' correctly
-- built dicts went unread.
--
-- 🚨 AND IT WAS DECIDED BY DECLARATION ORDER: with the two `impl Conv` blocks
-- swapped, the base printed `wrap-char-int/wrap-char-int` -- measured at
-- `e4587a04` on the byte-identical swapped twin `probes/p1956_swap.mdk`, not on
-- this file -- which DICT-SEMANTICS §3
-- forbids outright.  Section 4's permutation pair grades that half automatically.
--
-- ⚠️ THE REJECT SIBLING IS s-nary-given-nonlead-mismatch-rejected.mdk: a fix that
-- answered this goal by matching the LEAD argument alone would also answer that
-- one, and would hand its body a `Conv (Wrap Int) Int` dict to call at `Bool` --
-- so neither file is meaningful alone.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

interface Conv s t where
  conv : s -> t -> String

impl Conv (Wrap Int) Bool where
  conv _ _ = "wrap-int-bool"

impl Conv (Wrap Char) Int where
  conv _ _ = "wrap-char-int"

f : Conv (Wrap a) b => Wrap a -> b -> String
f w y = conv w y

main = println "\{f (Wrap 5) True}/\{f (Wrap 'c') 7}"
